{"version":1,"projection":".$mem","views":{"storage":"Memory of the Rust value/place itself. Available on API value terms, Rust fields and sequence elements, including opaque generic values. It is not the pointee memory of a pointer.","region":"A typed logical region designating exactly one pointee value. Obtained as p.$mem.pointee for a raw pointer or explicitly supported pointer wrapper. Constructing this observation does not dereference the pointer and remains possible for null/dangling/misaligned pointers.","allocation":"The originating allocation record, retained after deallocation. Identity includes allocation generation, so address reuse does not establish identity."},"fields":{"exists":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Whether the view has represented backing storage. start/size/align observations do not by themselves imply this flag."},"start":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Byte address of this view's beginning. For p.$mem it is the address of the pointer slot; for p.$mem.pointee it is the pointer's data address, including 0 for null."},"size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Byte size of the view's type: pointer-slot size for p.$mem, sizeof(T) for the region designated by *const T/*mut T. DST views use the full dynamic size. Nonnegative; never the containing allocation's capacity."},"end":{"type":"integer","meaning":"start + size on mathematical integers, without machine wrapping."},"align":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Positive byte alignment REQUIRED by the view's type, not proof that start satisfies it. Proper alignment is start % align == 0, also when size is zero."},"readable":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The whole size-byte view is valid for reads in the current state, respecting allocation provenance, liveness, range containment and access permission. Does not imply alignment or initialized/valid contents. Zero-byte read access is vacuous."},"writable":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The whole size-byte view is valid for writes in the current state, respecting allocation provenance, liveness, range containment and access permission. Does not imply alignment or initialized/valid contents. Zero-byte write access is vacuous."},"readable_size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Maximum nonnegative contiguous byte extent valid for reads from start in the current state, within one live provenance-compatible allocation. Zero if no positive extent is accessible. An n-byte read needs n <= readable_size for nonnegative n."},"writable_size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Maximum nonnegative contiguous byte extent valid for writes from start under the same range/provenance rules. An n-byte write needs n <= writable_size for nonnegative n."},"initialized":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Every byte of this size-byte view has been written/initialized, including padding. Does not imply a valid typed bit pattern, alignment, liveness or permission."},"valid":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The view represents a language-valid initialized value of its associated Rust type, including discriminants/niches and required initialized bytes. Allows uninitialized padding. This is the predicate for 'properly initialized value of T'; do NOT additionally require initialized. Does not imply library safety invariants, alignment, access permission or liveness."},"allocation":{"type":"allocation","meaning":"Originating allocation record. Never inferred merely by finding a currently live allocation at the same numeric address."}},"allocation_fields":{"exists":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Whether this pointer/place has an originating allocation record."},"id":{"type":"string","meaning":"Stable allocation-generation identity. Identity/bounds fields require an existing record; same-allocation formulas must establish existence before comparing IDs. Equal originating IDs alone do not imply pointer addresses lie within the allocation: an out-of-bounds derived pointer retains its originating ID."},"start":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Allocation beginning in bytes."},"size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Actual returned allocation size in bytes."},"end":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Allocation start + size."},"align":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Alignment guaranteed by this allocation's allocation contract."},"minimum_size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Minimum fitting-layout size retained from the allocation request/contract. Not derivable from actual capacity alone."},"live":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Record exists and this allocation generation is currently live."},"allocator":{"type":"string","meaning":"Allocator contract identity. This is not the numeric address of an allocator object's own storage."}},"pointer_wrappers":["core::ptr::non_null::NonNull","core::ptr::unique::Unique"],"rules":["A pointer safety rule about what src/dst points to must use src.$mem.pointee or dst.$mem.pointee, not the pointer slot's $mem fields.","The pointee view covers ONE T. A copy of count T values has byte length count * pointee.size. For variable-length accesses compare that length with readable_size/writable_size; overlap checks use that length and starts, not single-value end or entire allocation size.","Read/write access, alignment, byte initialization, typed validity and allocation identity are separate properties. Preserve precisely the supplied atomic obligation; do not silently add the others.","Provenance and containment are distinct. If a rule says pointers are within the same allocation, establish existing allocation records, equal allocation-generation IDs, and address bounds for both pointers. Pointer-arithmetic bounds allow one-past-the-end; do not require the entire pointee value to fit merely to compare byte positions. A rule that only asks equal origin IDs does not itself add containment or liveness.","All views describe the current observation state. They do not express future non-mutation, borrow lifetimes, data races, post-call states or library behavioral invariants.","Type/lifetime parameter handles and modeled-memory metadata scalars have no $mem. Literal